From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:53:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sleep: tell the woken core's faults apart
 by time

Make each entry of the resume stub's vectors read ESR_EL2 and restart
WD2 for 10 s on an instruction abort, 20 s on a data abort and 30 s
on any other class, so the reset time after a failed T8132 wake says
whether the confined core could not fetch, could not write, or
something else stopped it. A hang still takes the stub's 60 s.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
index 629753d500..917ce1077a 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
@@ -3311,8 +3311,9 @@ static void t8140_wake(struct apple_sleep *s)
  *
  * VBAR_EL2 still points at the Stage 2 firmware's vectors here, whose handler stays
  * silent, so a fault in the stub or early in cpu_resume used to end in the 60 s
- * watchdog like a hang. Take t8132_wake_vectors first: every entry restarts WD2 for
- * 10 s and waits, so a fault resets the Mac about 10 s after the wake instead of 60.
+ * watchdog like a hang. Take t8132_wake_vectors first: every entry restarts WD2 and
+ * waits, for 10 s on an instruction abort, 20 s on a data abort and 30 s on anything
+ * else, so the reset time says which, and a hang still takes the 60 s.
  * init_kernel_el sets the kernel's own vectors, as on a cold boot.
  */
 asm(
@@ -3348,13 +3349,23 @@ asm(
 "t8132_wake_vectors:\n"
 "	.rept	16\n"
 "	.balign	0x80\n"
-"	movz	x9, #0x882b, lsl #16\n"
+"	mrs	x10, esr_el2\n"
+"	ubfx	x10, x10, #26, #6\n"
+"	movz	w11, #0x5400\n"
+"	movk	w11, #0x2aea, lsl #16\n"
+"	cmp	x10, #0x21\n"
+"	b.ne	3f\n"
+"	movz	w11, #0x1c00\n"
+"	movk	w11, #0xe4e, lsl #16\n"
+"3:	cmp	x10, #0x25\n"
+"	b.ne	4f\n"
+"	movz	w11, #0x3800\n"
+"	movk	w11, #0x1c9c, lsl #16\n"
+"4:	movz	x9, #0x882b, lsl #16\n"
 "	movk	x9, #0x3, lsl #32\n"
 "	str	wzr, [x9, #0x2c]\n"
 "	str	wzr, [x9, #0x20]\n"
-"	movz	w10, #0x1c00\n"
-"	movk	w10, #0xe4e, lsl #16\n"
-"	str	w10, [x9, #0x28]\n"
+"	str	w11, [x9, #0x28]\n"
 "	mov	w10, #1\n"
 "	str	w10, [x9, #0x2c]\n"
 "2:	b	2b\n"
-- 
